            <description><![CDATA[The U.S. Army is moving ahead with plans to detonate a highly volatile explosive compound in Iowa. The lead azide is used in military munitions and has been deteriorating underground. The detonation could send a plume of toxic lead dust across the area, but Army officials insist a controlled explosion is the safest option. Geoff Bennett discussed more with Eliza Billingham of Iowa Public Radio.]]></description>
